Ischys — third-party attributions
================================

Ischys itself is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE).

Exercise catalog
----------------

`frontend/assets/catalog/catalog.json` (the bundled on-device exercise catalog,
736 exercises — names, muscles, categories, and how-to instruction text) is
derived from **free-exercise-db**:

    https://github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db

free-exercise-db is released into the public domain under **The Unlicense**.
No attribution is required; this notice is a courtesy.

Only catalog **metadata and instruction text** are bundled from it. Its exercise
**photographs are deliberately NOT used**: the Unlicense covers that project's
JSON, while the photographs are of unclear provenance — the upstream project
(`wrkout/exercises.json`) states they "have been scrapped off the internet" and
advises against commercial use. Ischys ships none of them.

Exercise artwork
----------------

The line-art exercise illustrations bundled in
`frontend/src/data/exerciseArt.generated.ts` are derived from **Workout Guide**:

    https://github.com/bryllim/workout-guide

Copyright (c) 2026 Bryl Lim. Licensed under the **Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International** license (CC BY-SA 4.0):

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

That artwork is itself derived from **Everkinetic** (https://everkinetic.com,
https://github.com/everkinetic/data), also licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.

Changes made by Ischys: the SVG frames were converted to bundled path data,
their fixed white fill was removed so the app tints them at runtime, and
coordinates were rounded to whole units to reduce size. No geometry was
otherwise altered. These adaptations are redistributed under the same
CC BY-SA 4.0 license.

The frames are regenerated by `frontend/scripts/build-exercise-art.mjs`, which
pins the upstream commit it fetched.

